@ 6.2.2.1.6 - Classical Arabic to Cypriot Arabic
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Borg, Alexander (1985), Cypriot Arabic NB: Changes may not be in chronological order. {θ,ð} {f,v} {x,ɣ} voicing neutralized “in contact with other fricatives” Epenthesis in medial CCC clusters, often so that the syllable break is between the second and third consonants
